BOM
AiMesh combines more than one ASUS router to form an AiMesh system, providing whole-home coverage and centralized management.
You can click the \"Search\" button on the network map to find your AiMesh node. <br>If there are any available AiMesh nodes nearby that can be added to your AiMesh system, they will appear in your available AiMesh node list.
If you cannot find any available AiMesh nodes nearby:
1. Please reset your AiMesh node and try again.
2. Make sure your AiMesh node is up to date. (Firmware version needs to support AiMesh)
Find supported firmware
The AiMesh system is composed of ASUS routers. One router will become the AiMesh router and you can add additional AiMesh nodes to expand your network.
Connect your modem to the WAN port on your router using the Ethernet cable.
I want to set this device as an AiMesh node
Press [Next] button to reset this AiMesh node, and then place the AiMesh node stand by near your AiMesh router.
Re-connect your AiMesh router to your mobile/NB/PC.
I want to set this device as an AiMesh router
Please connect your mobile/NB/PC to your AiMesh router.
Congratulations! RT-AX53U can be added to your AiMesh system.
Your AiMesh node is going to be reset to default, please re-direct your mobile/NB/PC to your AiMesh router
Your AiMesh node is going to be reset to its default settings and then will proceed to next process, are you sure you want to continue?
If you cannot find your AiMesh router nearby. Please make sure your current mobile/NB/PC is already connected to your AiMesh router by an Ethernet cable or WiFi.
When using wired, use an Ethernet cable to connect the LAN port of your AiMesh router to your current NB/PC.
When using WiFi, search the network name (SSID) of your AiMesh router with your mobile/NB/PC, and connect it.
Please log in AiMesh router and then add this AiMesh node to your AiMesh system.
You can add AiMesh nodes to form an AiMesh WiFi system to provide extra WiFi coverage.
You can set this router as an AiMesh node to extend an existing AiMesh routers WiFi coverage.
Factory resetting this router will allow it to join an existing AiMesh network.
Please go to the AiMesh settings page of your existing router to add an AiMesh node.
Changes made to your wireless settings will affect your mesh network!
Do you want to add another node?
Add another node
is now used as dedicated WiFi backhaul under AiMesh mode.
