If you want to hardwire your AiMesh router and AiMesh node together, please connect your RJ-45 cable to the LAN port of the AiMesh router and the WAN port of your AiMesh node. The AiMesh system will automatically switch to an Ethernet backhaul.
Connection Priority
Auto will change your system's connection type between wired or wireless automatically.
Ethernet will change your system's connection type to wired.
The system will adapt the connection type between wired or wireless based on the current connection quality/status.
Ethernet first
The system will prioritize Ethernet connection.
When Ethernet backhaul mode is enabled, the system will use only wired connection as Ethernet backhaul.
You can choose auto (Ethernet-based) to use one of the WANs or the preferred WAN port.
Ethernet only
Ethernet-based
Powerline first
WiFi first
Please make sure your uplink AP support the backhaul connection type you prefer to use.
If the uplink AP does not support the connection type, you might encounter an unstable connection or even disconnection.
Backhaul Connection Priority
The system will always prioritize WiFi backhaul connection even when Ethernet backhaul is available.
The system will prioritize #CONNTYPE connection.
It will switch to WiFi backhaul when #CONNTYPE connection is no longer available.
#CONNPRIOTYPE first
#CONNPRIOTYPE only
AiMesh Wireless Backhaul
Use as both backhaul and fronthaul connection
Use as a dedicated wireless backhaul
Release for fronthaul connection when wireless backhaul is not active
