Your wireless network is insecure because you have not set up a wireless password. Click here to change your Authentication Method and set a WPA Pre-Shared Key password.
Disable UPnP services to prevent your router settings being altered by programs using the UPnP port. If you are using anything that requires dynamic port forwarding, keep UPnP enabled.
Disable web access from WAN connections to prevent external control of your router.
Disable PING from WAN to avoid cracker can connect to router from external network.
Disable DMZ to avoid all the inbounds packets are redirected to the computer exposing on internet.
Disable Port trigger to prevent your router from cracker access via specific port.
Disable Port forwarding to prevent your router from cracker access via specific port.
Disable Anonymous login to FTP share to avoid unauthorized user have chance to access your data.
Disable guest login for Network Place Share to avoid unauthorized user have chance to access your data.
Enable Malicious Website Blocking to restrict access to malicious websites recorded in our database.
Enable Vulnerability Protection to prevent cracker invasion via vulnerability of router or device software.
Enable Intefected Device Prevention and Blocking to detect any suspicious connections or activities, and block them to prevent data stealing.
Disable WiFi Protected Setup to prevent attackers from obtaining your keys via an intelligent brute force attack.
