RT-AX53U provides Dual WAN support. Select Failover mode to use a secondary WAN for backup network access. Select Load Balance mode to optimize bandwidth, maximize throughput, minimize response time, and prevent data overload for both WAN connections.
Enable Dual WAN
Allow failback
The time period criteria to trigger failback mechanism. When you change to the secondary WAN, the router will check how long primary WAN is connected. If the primary WAN connection is stable (longer than failback detect time), the connection will change to primary WAN.
When the Primary WAN is detected to have an active internet connection using a physical cable for $WANDOG_FB_COUNT continuous times, failback to the Primary WAN.
Failback Trigger Condition
When the current WAN fails $WANDOG_MAXFAIL continuous times, failover to Secondary WAN
When the current WAN fails $WANDOG_MAXFAIL continuous times, it is deemed a disconnection.
Failover Trigger Condition
If the primary WAN is not &#39;Ethernet LAN&#39;, IPTV function will be disable. Are you sure to process?
