Using IFTTT with ASUS Router
IFTTT is short for "if this then that." It is a platform that connects websites, apps, and Internet-connected devices with simple conditional statements, called “Applets”. The Applet uses specific conditions to perform all kinds of custom tasks for you. Connect ASUS Router to IFTTT and start an automation life with creative applets on ASUS Router channel. For example:
If closes to dinner time or bedtime, then turn off WiFi
If my daughter comes home, then send me and email, text, or phone call
If my wife comes home, then play my favorite song
If I am playing a game, then boost the game speed
More Applets
To manually pair ASUS Router with IFTTT, please copy and paste the activation code below onto the Link ASUS Router and IFTTT webpage.
Choose from the existing applets or create your own applets on <a id="ifttt_applet_link">ASUS Router Channel</a>
<a id="ifttt_signin">Sign in</a> to your IFTTT account.
Start an automation life with ASUS Router and IFTTT!
