Additional pppd options
Host Name
Internet Detection
<b>Disable:</b> Disable it to turn off Internet Detection. <b>PPP Echo:</b> Use Echo-Request and Echo-Reply message defined in PPP Link Control Protocol (LCP) to test the PPP connection. <b>DNS Probe:</b> Performs a DNS lookup request and resolved IP address to test DNS connection.
MAC Address
PPP Echo Interval
Send an LCP Echo-Request frame to the peer every n seconds.
PPP Echo Max Failures
Presume the peer to be dead if n LCP Echo-Requests are sent without receiving a valid LCP Echo-Reply. Use of this option requires a non-zero value for the Echo Interval parameter.
DNS Probe Max Failures
If DNS resolution fails or returns the wrong address to n times, then it is assumed that the internet connection is completely unsuccessful.
The Maximum Receive Unit (MRU) of PPPoE packet. The default value is 1492. Change this value only if your ISP requires it.
MRU
The Maximum Transmission Unit (MTU) of PPPoE packet. The default value is 1492. Change this value only if your ISP requires it.
MTU
