When you're using IKEv1 Aggressive mode, the authentication hash based on a PSK is transmitted as response to the initial packet of the VPN client that wants to establish an IPSec Tunnel. The hash PSK is not encrypted. An attacker can do offline dictionary and brute-force attacks against it to recover the PSK. So please avoid using the Aggressive mode.
