WAN aggregation
WAN Aggregation combines two network connections to increase your WAN speed up to 2Gbps. Connect your router's #WAN port and LAN 4 port to your modem's LAN ports (ensure you use two cables with the same specification). <a id="wanAgg_faq" target="_blank" style="color:#FFCC00;text-decoration:underline;">WAN Aggregation FAQ</a>
Enable WAN Aggregation
Your router has Dual WAN enabled. Enabling WAN Aggregation will disable Dual WAN. Are you sure you want to continue?
Your router has WAN Aggregation enabled. Enabling Dual WAN will disable WAN Aggregation. Are you sure you want to continue?
WAN Aggregation is using your router's LAN 4 port. Enabling IPTV will disable WAN Aggregation. Are you sure you want to continue?
IPTV is using your router's LAN 4 port. Enabling WAN Aggregation will disable IPTV. Are you sure you want to continue?
Your router has both Dual WAN and IPTV enabled. Enabling WAN Aggregation will disable Dual WAN and IPTV to avoid port conflicts. Are you sure you want to continue?
Ensure your router's #WAN port and your modem's LAN port have been connected using two cables with the same specification.
Ensure your router's LAN 4 port and your modem's LAN port have been connected using two cables with the same specification.
To enable WAN Aggregation go to the <a href="Advanced_WAN_Content.asp" style="color:#FFCC00;text-decoration:underline;">WAN-Internet Connection page</a>.
If WAN Aggregation setup is not successful, please follow the steps below to retry.
Make sure your modem’s LAN ports have already connected to your router’s #WAN and LAN 4 with cables.
Make sure your modem has enabled 802.3ad
Confirm that you use two cables with the same spec (either gigabit & gigabit or 10/100& 10/100Mbps)
Reboot your router
If the steps above are unsuccessful, please report this issue on the <a href='https://www.asus.com/support/' target='_blank' style='color:#000;text-decoration:underline;'>ASUS Support Site</a>.
WAN Aggregation does not support WAN types such as PPPoE, PPTP, and L2TP. If your WAN type changes to PPPoE, PPTP, or L2TP, WAN aggregation will be disabled automatically. Are you sure you want to continue?
