This item allows you to select any of these options for the Wireless Mode of your 802.11n interface. <p>[Auto]: Allows 802.11n, 802.11g, and 802.11b devices to connect to RT-AX53U.</p><p>[Legacy]: Allows 802.11b/g/n devices to connect to RT-AX53U, but 802.11n devices only run at a speed of 54Mbps. Please select Legacy mode if you want to get more options for the authentication method.</p><p>[N Only]: Maximizes performance, but does not allow 802.11g and 802.11b devices to connect to your device.</p><p>Tick b/g Protection to allow b/g devices to connect to RT-AX53U without affecting 11n devices, but this increases the router's workload.</p>
This item allows you to select any of these options for the Wireless Mode of your 802.11n interface. <p>[Auto]: Allows 802.11n and 802.11a devices to connect to RT-AX53U.</p><p>[Legacy]: Allows 802.11n/a devices to connect to RT-AX53U, but 802.11n devices only run at a speed of 54Mbps. Please select Legacy mode if you want to get more options for the authentication method.</p><p>[N Only]: Maximizes performance, but does not allow 802.11a devices to connect to your device.</p>
This item allows you to select any of these options for the Wireless Mode of your 802.11ac interface. <p>[Auto]: Allows 802.11ac, 802.11n and 802.11a devices to connect to RT-AX53U.</p><p>[Legacy]: Allows 802.11n/a devices to connect to RT-AX53U, but 802.11n devices only run at a speed of 54Mbps. Please select Legacy mode if you want to get more options for the authentication method.</p><p>[N + AC]: Maximizes performance, but does not allow 802.11a devices to connect to your device.</p>
This item allows you to select any of these options for the Wireless Mode of your 802.11ac interface. <p>[Auto]: Allows 802.11ac, 802.11n and 802.11a devices to connect to RT-AX53U.</p><p>[N Only]: 802.11n maximizes performance, but does not allow 802.11ac, 802.11a devices to connect to your device.</p>
This item allows you to select any of these options for the Wireless Mode of your 802.11ac interface. <p>[Auto]: Allows 802.11ac, 802.11n and 802.11a devices to connect to RT-AX53U.</p><p>[Legacy]: Allows 802.11n/a devices to connect to RT-AX53U, but 802.11n devices only run at a speed of 54Mbps. Please select Legacy mode if you want to get more options for the authentication method.</p><p>[N/AC mixed]: Maximizes performance, but does not allow 802.11a devices to connect to your device.</p><p>[N Only]: 802.11n maximizes performance, but does not allow 802.11ac, 802.11a devices to connect to your device.</p>
