VPN Fusion
allows you to connect to multiple VPN servers simultaneously and assign your client devices to connect to different VPN tunnels. Some devices like set-top boxes, smart TVs and Blu-ray players do not support VPN software. This feature provides VPN access to such devices in a home network without having to install VPN software, while your smartphone remains connected to Internet not VPN.
For Gamer, VPN connection counteracts DDoS attacks to prevent your PC game or your stream from disconnecting with game servers. Building a VPN connection also can simply change your IP address to the region where the game server is located, to improve your ping to game servers.
To start, please follow the steps below:
Click the "+" button beside Server List to add a new VPN tunnel.
Activate the VPN connection you created in Server List.
Click the "+" button beside Exception List and select the online client you want to configure.
Assign a VPN connection to the client device, and click OK.
Activate the VPN policy in Exception List, and click Apply at the bottom of the page.
Server List
Allows you to create VPN connection profiles. The max number of concurrent active VPN connections is 4.
Connection Name
Activate
Editor
Exception List
You can add VPN policies to the exception list, so that different client devices can connect to different VPN tunnels.
The client device not in the exception list will connect to the default VPN tunnel. You can set the default VPN tunnel after the VPN profile is created. When the default VPN tunnel is disconnected or deactivated, the client device not in the exception list will connect to Internet not VPN.
Please deactivate the profile before editing it.
Please deactivate the profile before deleting it.
All policy exceptions set for a VPN profile will be removed when the profile is deleted. Are you sure you want to delete the profile?
Are you sure you want to delete this profile?
Deleting the client's policy in the exception list will also delete the client's IP binding of the DHCP Server. Are you sure you want to delete this?
Remove the client&#39;s IP binding will also delete the client&#39;s policy in the exception list of VPN Fusion. Are you sure you want to delete?
